full_question:
Refer to the nextIntInRangemethod below:
 /** @return a random integer in the range low to high, inclusive */
 public int nextIntInRange(int low, int high)
 {
 return /* expression */
 }
 Which /* expression */ will always return a value that satisfies the postcondition? Options: 1. (int) (Math.random() * high) + low;, 2. (int) (Math.random() * (high - low)) + low;, 3. (int) (Math.random() * (high - low + 1)) + low;, 4. (int) (Math.random() * (high + low)) + low;

In the program below, y is a positive integer (e.g. l, 2, 3, ...).
 result ← 0
 REPEAT 3 TIMES {
 REPEAT y TIMES {
 result ← result + 1
 }
 } Options: 1. y+3, 2. 3y, 3. y^3, 4. 3^y
